### Payments Ledger: one example call per endpoint.
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension. In IntelliJ's HTTP Client, replace the
### {{name.response.body.x}} references with variables set in a response handler, for example:
###   > {% client.global.set("aliceToken", response.body.access_token); %}
###
### Start the dependencies first: `docker compose up -d postgres keycloak`, then `./mvnw spring-boot:run`.
### Run the requests top to bottom: later ones use ids and tokens captured from earlier ones.
### The interactive docs are at http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html (click Authorize and paste a token).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@keycloak = http://localhost:8081

### 1. Get a local token from Keycloak (password grant, DEVELOPMENT ONLY).
### Users come from keycloak/ledger-realm.json; these passwords are local-dev values and must never be
### used anywhere else:
###   alice      / alice-dev-password   (USER)
###   bob        / bob-dev-password     (USER)
###   admin-user / admin-dev-password   (ADMIN)
### The token lives 15 minutes: when a request returns 401, run the login again.

# @name loginAlice
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/ledger/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ledger-api&username=alice&password=alice-dev-password

###
# @name loginBob
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/ledger/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ledger-api&username=bob&password=bob-dev-password

###
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/ledger/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ledger-api&username=admin-user&password=admin-dev-password

### 2. Reuse the token: send it as `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`. The variables below read it from
### the login responses above.

@aliceToken = {{loginAlice.response.body.access_token}}
@bobToken = {{loginBob.response.body.access_token}}
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.access_token}}

### Same thing with curl, for reference:
###   TOKEN=$(curl -s -d grant_type=password -d client_id=ledger-api -d username=alice \
###     -d password=alice-dev-password http://localhost:8081/realms/ledger/protocol/openid-connect/token \
###     | jq -r .access_token)
###   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" http://localhost:8080/accounts

### Health (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### POST /accounts: open an account for the caller (alice, EUR)
# @name aliceAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "EUR" }

### POST /accounts: open an account for the caller (bob, EUR)
# @name bobAccount
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currency": "EUR" }

### GET /accounts: your accounts (an ADMIN sees all)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### GET /accounts/{id}
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{aliceAccount.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### POST /accounts/{id}/deposits: ADMIN only, needs an Idempotency-Key.
### Amounts are minor units: 15000 = 150.00 EUR.
### Sending this twice with the same key returns the same response plus `Idempotency-Replayed: true`.
### A failed request stores nothing under its key, so a retry with the same key runs again.
POST {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{aliceAccount.response.body.id}}/deposits
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: dev-deposit-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 15000, "currency": "EUR" }

### GET /accounts/{id}/balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{aliceAccount.response.body.id}}/balance
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### POST /transfers: alice sends 25.00 EUR to bob. Use a new Idempotency-Key for each new transfer.
# @name transfer
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Idempotency-Key: dev-transfer-0001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": {{aliceAccount.response.body.id}},
  "targetAccountId": {{bobAccount.response.body.id}},
  "amount": 2500,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### GET /transfers/{id}: visible to its parties and to an ADMIN
GET {{baseUrl}}/transfers/{{transfer.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken}}

### GET /accounts/{id}/transactions: ledger entries, paged (page, size, sort, from, to)
GET {{baseUrl}}/accounts/{{aliceAccount.response.body.id}}/transactions?page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

### POST /transfers/{id}/reverse: ADMIN only, needs an Idempotency-Key, no body
POST {{baseUrl}}/transfers/{{transfer.response.body.id}}/reverse
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Idempotency-Key: dev-reverse-0001

### POST /admin/reconciliation: ADMIN only, read-only consistency check
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/reconciliation
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### The API description (public): JSON for tooling, Swagger UI for people
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs
